# Cursor Rules for NextJS + Supabase + Tailwind Project

## Tech Stack
- NextJS 14+ with App Router
- TypeScript (strict mode)
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Supabase for backend (auth, database, storage)
- shadcn/ui for components
- Framer Motion for animations
- Zod for validation
- React Hook Form for forms

## Code Style and Structure

### General Rules
- Always use TypeScript with proper type definitions
- Prefer functional components with hooks over class components
- Use async/await over .then() chains
- Include error handling in all async operations
- Write self-documenting code with clear variable names
- Keep components small and focused (single responsibility)

### File Naming Conventions
- Components: PascalCase (e.g., `RecipeCard.tsx`)
- Utilities/Hooks: camelCase (e.g., `useRecipes.ts`, `formatDate.ts`)
- Types/Interfaces: PascalCase with descriptive names
- API routes: kebab-case (e.g., `api/get-recipes/route.ts`)

### Project Structure
```
src/
├── app/                    # NextJS app router pages
│   ├── (auth)/            # Auth group routes
│   ├── (dashboard)/       # Protected routes
│   └── api/               # API routes
├── components/
│   ├── ui/                # shadcn/ui components
│   ├── forms/             # Form components
│   ├── layouts/           # Layout components
│   └── features/          # Feature-specific components
├── lib/
│   ├── supabase/          # Supabase client and queries
│   ├── utils/             # Utility functions
│   └── validations/       # Zod schemas
├── hooks/                 # Custom React hooks
├── types/                 # TypeScript type definitions
└── styles/               # Global styles
```

## NextJS Specific Rules

### App Router Best Practices
- Use server components by default, client components only when needed
- Add "use client" directive only for interactive components
- Implement proper loading.tsx and error.tsx for each route
- Use metadata exports for SEO
- Leverage parallel routes and intercepting routes where applicable

### Data Fetching
```typescript
// Server Component - Preferred for data fetching
async function RecipePage({ params }: { params: { id: string } }) {
  const recipe = await getRecipe(params.id)
  return <RecipeDetail recipe={recipe} />
}

// Client Component - Only when needed for interactivity
"use client"
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react'

function InteractiveRecipeList() {
  // Client-side data fetching only when necessary
}
```

### API Routes
```typescript
// app/api/recipes/route.ts
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from 'next/server'
import { createRouteHandlerClient } from '@supabase/auth-helpers-nextjs'
import { cookies } from 'next/headers'

export async function GET(request: NextRequest) {
  try {
    const supabase = createRouteHandlerClient({ cookies })
    // Implementation
    return NextResponse.json({ data })
  } catch (error) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: error.message }, { status: 500 })
  }
}
```

## Supabase Integration

### Client Setup
```typescript
// lib/supabase/client.ts
import { createBrowserClient } from '@supabase/auth-helpers-nextjs'
import type { Database } from '@/types/database.types'

export const createClient = () =>
  createBrowserClient<Database>(
    process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL!,
    process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY!
  )
```

### Database Queries
- Always use TypeScript types generated from Supabase
- Implement Row Level Security (RLS) policies
- Use proper error handling
- Create reusable query functions

```typescript
// lib/supabase/queries/recipes.ts
import { createClient } from '../client'
import type { Recipe } from '@/types/database.types'

export async function getRecipes(filters?: RecipeFilters) {
  const supabase = createClient()
  
  const { data, error } = await supabase
    .from('recipes')
    .select(`
      *,
      users (
        id,
        display_name,
        avatar_url
      ),
      ingredients (*),
      reviews (
        rating
      )
    `)
    .order('created_at', { ascending: false })
  
  if (error) throw error
  return data as Recipe[]
}
```

### Authentication
```typescript
// Always check auth status in server components
import { createServerComponentClient } from '@supabase/auth-helpers-nextjs'
import { cookies } from 'next/headers'
import { redirect } from 'next/navigation'

export default async function ProtectedPage() {
  const supabase = createServerComponentClient({ cookies })
  const { data: { session } } = await supabase.auth.getSession()
  
  if (!session) {
    redirect('/login')
  }
  
  // Page content
}
```

## Tailwind CSS & Styling

### Class Organization
- Use Tailwind classes in logical order: layout → spacing → typography → colors → effects
- Prefer Tailwind utilities over custom CSS
- Use cn() utility for conditional classes

```typescript
// lib/utils.ts
import { clsx, type ClassValue } from 'clsx'
import { twMerge } from 'tailwind-merge'

export function cn(...inputs: ClassValue[]) {
  return twMerge(clsx(inputs))
}

// Usage in components
<div className={cn(
  "flex items-center justify-between p-4",
  "bg-white dark:bg-gray-900",
  "rounded-lg shadow-sm",
  isActive && "ring-2 ring-blue-500"
)} />
```

### Responsive Design
- Always design mobile-first
- Use responsive prefixes consistently
```typescript
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
```

### Dark Mode
- Implement dark mode support using Tailwind's dark: prefix
- Use CSS variables for theme colors

## Component Patterns

### Reusable Components
```typescript
// components/ui/Button.tsx
import { forwardRef } from 'react'
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils'

interface ButtonProps extends React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement> {
  variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'ghost'
  size?: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg'
  isLoading?: boolean
}

export const Button = forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, ButtonProps>(
  ({ className, variant = 'primary', size = 'md', isLoading, children, disabled, ...props }, ref) => {
    return (
      <button
        ref={ref}
        disabled={disabled || isLoading}
        className={cn(
          'inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md font-medium transition-colors',
          'focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2',
          'disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50',
          // variant styles
          variant === 'primary' && 'bg-blue-600 text-white hover:bg-blue-700',
          // size styles
          size === 'sm' && 'h-8 px-3 text-sm',
          size === 'md' && 'h-10 px-4',
          size === 'lg' && 'h-12 px-6',
          className
        )}
        {...props}
      >
        {isLoading ? <Spinner className="mr-2" /> : null}
        {children}
      </button>
    )
  }
)

Button.displayName = 'Button'
```

### Custom Hooks
```typescript
// hooks/useRecipes.ts
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react'
import { getRecipes } from '@/lib/supabase/queries/recipes'
import type { Recipe } from '@/types/database.types'

export function useRecipes(filters?: RecipeFilters) {
  const [recipes, setRecipes] = useState<Recipe[]>([])
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true)
  const [error, setError] = useState<Error | null>(null)

  useEffect(() => {
    const fetchRecipes = async () => {
      try {
        setIsLoading(true)
        const data = await getRecipes(filters)
        setRecipes(data)
      } catch (err) {
        setError(err as Error)
      } finally {
        setIsLoading(false)
      }
    }

    fetchRecipes()
  }, [filters])

  return { recipes, isLoading, error }
}
```

## Form Handling

### With React Hook Form + Zod
```typescript
// lib/validations/recipe.ts
import { z } from 'zod'

export const recipeSchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(3, 'Title must be at least 3 characters'),
  description: z.string().min(10, 'Description must be at least 10 characters'),
  prepTime: z.number().min(0),
  cookTime: z.number().min(0),
  servings: z.number().min(1),
  ingredients: z.array(z.object({
    name: z.string(),
    amount: z.string(),
    unit: z.string()
  })).min(1, 'At least one ingredient is required'),
})

export type RecipeFormData = z.infer<typeof recipeSchema>

// components/forms/RecipeForm.tsx
"use client"
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form'
import { zodResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/zod'
import { recipeSchema, type RecipeFormData } from '@/lib/validations/recipe'

export function RecipeForm() {
  const form = useForm<RecipeFormData>({
    resolver: zodResolver(recipeSchema),
    defaultValues: {
      title: '',
      ingredients: [{ name: '', amount: '', unit: '' }]
    }
  })

  const onSubmit = async (data: RecipeFormData) => {
    try {
      // Submit logic
    } catch (error) {
      // Error handling
    }
  }

  return (
    <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
      {/* Form fields */}
    </form>
  )
}
```

## Error Handling

### Consistent Error Boundaries
```typescript
// app/error.tsx
'use client'

export default function Error({
  error,
  reset,
}: {
  error: Error & { digest?: string }
  reset: () => void
}) {
  return (
    <div className="flex min-h-screen flex-col items-center justify-center">
      <h2 className="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold">Something went wrong!</h2>
      <button
        onClick={reset}
        className="rounded-md bg-blue-600 px-4 py-2 text-white hover:bg-blue-700"
      >
        Try again
      </button>
    </div>
  )
}
```

### API Error Responses
```typescript
// Consistent error format
export function handleApiError(error: unknown) {
  console.error('API Error:', error)
  
  if (error instanceof Error) {
    return NextResponse.json(
      { error: error.message },
      { status: 400 }
    )
  }
  
  return NextResponse.json(
    { error: 'An unexpected error occurred' },
    { status: 500 }
  )
}
```

